      "reason": "Carry the upstream SSH stdio ProxyCommand mode and shared CONNECT bridge instead of an ALab tunnel implementation. Full ten-file review follows CLI cloud/application-policy admission, ChatGPT OAuth-only login, exact built-in HTTPS gateway origin checks before polling the token future, sensitive bearer headers, binary stdio, input half-close and remote EOF completion. OpenSSH retains SSH authentication and host-key verification. Listener mode retains loopback/trusted-origin admission and no TCP replay; Portals ERS credentials now require v2 on startup and renewal, with signature verification still the gateway responsibility. Linux SSH disables UDP segmentation offload for the stated transport issue. Full new/migrated tests reviewed, including route refusal before token lookup, byte relay, status-only CONNECT rejection and CLI policy rejection. Not yet merged or executed natively.",
